[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3 uid="uid://ctzelemgbuffer1"]

; THE G-BUFFER SCENE. Same shape as boulevard_shots.tscn and for the same reasons:
; the world builds itself, the exporter makes its own SubViewport and photographs the
; world through that, and the visible window renders nothing but the clear colour --
; so no pixel outside this process is ever read.
;
; TZELEM then loads what this writes with tzelem/gbuffer.py and does not need to know
; an engine was involved: the dict it gets back has the same keys and shapes as our
; own numpy stage.gbuffer().

